# DLC mu=0.4 speed sweep — 2026-11-10

CarSim dataset: `Run_4d669775` (`DLC80_mu0.5_PMPC`, name kept from the old
setup; the actual DLC friction is now **0.4**).

## How mu=0.4 was set

- Split-mu friction map `RdMu_c76da67c-...par`, table `#DiagramTwo0`:
  changed the test-pad value from 0.5 to 0.4; name changed to
  `Mu = 0.4 Test Pad; 0.85 Everywhere Else`.
- The inlined friction table in
  `Results\Run_4d669775\Run_all.par` was also changed to 0.4.
- Initial speed was set equal to target by setting the CarSim
  procedure/run-control `*SPEED` and confirming `SV_VXS` in the run par;
  `Vx` logs start at the target speed.
- Original 0.5 friction par backup:
  `C:\Users\user\AppData\Local\Temp\opencode\jt_run\RdMu_c76_mu05_backup.par`.

## Sweep results (ey max / RMS, m)

| Initial = target | MPC | ZENG | Proposed | Note |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| 60 | 0.600 / 0.180 | 0.594 / 0.174 | **0.558 / 0.169** | easy; 10 s covers 160 m, not full path |
| **70** | **0.750 / 0.345** | **0.814 / 0.367** | **0.631 / 0.252** | all controlled; Proposed best |
| 75 | 2.463 / 1.095 | 1.163 / 0.548 | **0.743 / 0.293** | MPC saturates; boundary |
| 80 | 6.031 / 2.585 | **0.906 / 0.398** | 1.010 / 0.349 | MPC fails; ZENG max best, Proposed RMS/SW/beta best |

All QP success rates 100%.

## Recommended: 70 km/h

70 km/h is the highest speed where all three controllers remain controlled.
Full metrics:

| Controller | ey max | ey RMS | ey final | SW max | Mz max | Md max | beta max | yaw max | LTR max | QP |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| MPC | 0.750 | 0.345 | 0.051 | 429.7 | 2768 | 1553 | 2.27 | 15.2 | 0.41 | 100% |
| ZENG | 0.814 | 0.367 | 0.175 | 525.0 | 2906 | 1626 | 2.47 | 16.2 | 0.44 | 100% |
| **Proposed** | **0.631** | **0.252** | **0.027** | **87.0** | 2876 | **1389** | **1.73** | **13.8** | **0.39** | **100%** |

Relative to MPC:

- `ey max -15.9%`
- `ey RMS -27.0%`
- `SW max -79.8%`
- `beta max -23.8%`
- `Md max -10.6%`
- `LTR -4.9%`
- `Mz max` +3.9% (slightly worse)

Relative to ZENG:

- `ey max -22.5%`
- `ey RMS -31.3%`
- `SW max -83.4%`
- `beta max -30.0%`
- `Md max -14.6%`
- `yaw max -14.8%`
- `LTR -11.4%`

## Why 70, not 75/80/60

- 60: all easy, little discrimination; 10 s run does not reach the full path.
- 70: all controlled; Proposed clearly best. **Recommended main comparison.**
- 75: MPC already saturates (`2.46 m`, SW 720°); boundary case.
- 80: MPC fails (`6.03 m`); ZENG max `0.906` is slightly better than
  Proposed `1.010`, while Proposed is better on RMS/SW/beta. Not a clean win.

## Proposed parameters used

- DLC `Q_epsi=5`
- `Wb=10`
- `w2_max=w1_max=2e3`
- `w2_gain=w1_gain=3`
- `R2=200`

